# Sent on every request to the Discogs API. Discogs rejects requests without a
# descriptive User-Agent, so set this to something identifying your deployment.
DISCOGS_USER_AGENT="Crate/1.0 +https://your-app.vercel.app"

# --- Sign in with Discogs (OAuth 1.0a) ---------------------------------------
# Set both to add a "Sign in with Discogs" button, so visitors authorise the app
# instead of pasting a token. Leave either unset and the button never appears.
#
# Create an application at https://www.discogs.com/settings/developers to get
# these. Discogs does not require the callback URL to be registered — in
# development the app derives it from the incoming request, so localhost works
# without extra configuration. In production you must pin it with
# DISCOGS_APP_URL below.
#
# The consumer secret signs every request. Treat it like any other secret:
# never commit it, and rotate it if it leaks.
DISCOGS_CONSUMER_KEY=""
DISCOGS_CONSUMER_SECRET=""

# The origin used to build the OAuth callback URL. REQUIRED in production
# whenever the consumer key and secret above are set — "Sign in with Discogs"
# refuses to start without it, rather than trusting the request's host headers.
#
# Next resolves the request origin from Host / X-Forwarded-Host. A proxy that
# forwards a forged one would let an attacker register a callback on their own
# host while holding the matching request token secret — both halves needed to
# complete another user's sign-in. Pinning the origin removes the question.
# DISCOGS_APP_URL="https://your-app.vercel.app"

# --- Demo mode ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional. Set this to a Discogs personal access token to offer a "take a look
# around a demo crate" button on the sign-in screen, letting visitors browse
# that account's collection without signing in at all.
#
# Read server-side on every request and never sent to a browser — the demo
# session cookie holds only a marker, not the token.
#
# Before enabling it, note that anyone using the demo:
#   - sees that account's username and its entire collection,
#   - spends that account's Discogs rate limit (60 requests/minute).
# A Discogs personal access token also grants *write* access to the account it
# belongs to, so prefer a token from a secondary account you don't mind sharing
# a view of, and never commit the value.
# DISCOGS_DEMO_TOKEN=""
